# Settings keyboard focus path. Run headed with a fresh TURNSTONE_ROOT, a TURNSTONE_CAPTURE_DIR
# and TURNSTONE_A11Y_PUBLIC_FIXTURE_RECEIPT=1 (labels in the tree), then:
#   scripts/check-settings-focus.py <capture dir>
# A click enters the Settings controls (key tab alone leaves focus on the window); each key
# press is followed by a tree snapshot whose focus_node_id the script reads. The scenario's
# own asserts only cover that input goes to the pane; the order and wrap checks are the script's.
settle 20
key escape
resize 1180 950
open mere://settings-reactive
settle 10
act id:pane:settings
settle 5
assert pane turnstone.settings
act Maximize pane
settle 4
click surface:settings role:button Reload saved
settle 3
assert focus pane
record-uxtree f00
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree f01
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree f02
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree f03
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree f04
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree f05
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree f06
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree f07
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree f08
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree f09
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree f10
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree f11
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree f12
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree f13
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree f14
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree f15
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree f16
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree f17
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree f18
key tab
settle 2
record-uxtree f19
key shift+tab
settle 2
record-uxtree b01
key shift+tab
settle 2
record-uxtree b02
key shift+tab
settle 2
record-uxtree b03
assert focus pane
log Settings focus walk recorded; run scripts/check-settings-focus.py on the capture dir
